    {
      "tag": "21+",
      "h2": "Backwards Numbers",
      "body_html": "<p>German says digits backwards! <strong>21 = einundzwanzig</strong> (one-and-twenty). 35 = funfunddreissig (five-and-thirty). Keep practising — it gets natural.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Age",
      "h2": "Saying Age",
      "body_html": "<p>'Ich bin 13 Jahre alt' = <strong>I am 13 years old</strong>. <strong>Ich bin</strong> = I am. Notice you use 'I am' here (unlike French 'I have').</p>"
    }
